  "answer": "No. The Microsoft Teams collaboration-channel connector is not generally available to all customers now. Its current phase is \"Under Active Design and Planning\" [NL-014#NL-014-S07], and a restricted pilot is planned to begin in October 2026 with selected financial and healthcare enterprise accounts before general release [NL-014#NL-014-S07]. The planned release window is Q4 2026, with v2.11.0 targeting November 24, 2026 [NL-014#NL-014-S04]. Sales statements implying it is nearly ready are overclaims; the official roadmap says it is in design/planned for Q4 2026 and not generally available [NL-023#NL-023-S04], and the existing internal demo lacks tenant isolation, permission mapping, SSO, and formatting, making it unsuitable for deployment [NL-027#NL-027-S03].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
